    "steps": [
      {
        "text": "Mix the soy sauce, calamansi juice, garlic, sugar and pepper in a bowl. Add the beef, massage the marinade in and leave it for at least 30 minutes.",
        "minutes": 30
      },
      {
        "text": "Make the garlic rice: break up the cold rice with wet hands. Heat the oil and garlic in a wok over medium-low heat until the garlic is golden, then add the rice and salt, raise the heat and toss until hot and lightly toasted.",
        "minutes": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Put the beef, its marinade and the water in a wide skillet over medium heat. Simmer, stirring now and then, until the liquid has evaporated.",
        "minutes": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Add the oil to the skillet and fry the beef, turning, until browned and caramelized at the edges. Watch it closely: the sugar burns quickly.",
        "minutes": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "Fry the eggs in the oil over medium heat, spooning hot oil over the whites until they set while the yolks stay runny. Season with a pinch of salt.",
        "minutes": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Divide the rice, tapa and eggs among plates. Serve with the spiced vinegar for dipping and sliced tomatoes.",
        "minutes": null
      }
    ],
    "tips": "For deeper flavor, marinate the beef overnight in the fridge. Freezing the beef for 30 minutes first makes it much easier to slice thin."
